<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Roatán</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Roatán is the largest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-islands">Bay Islands</a> of Honduras, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> Sea. In 1797 the British landed about 2,000 deported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garifuna">Garifuna</a> there, from where they spread along the Central American coast. English-speaking settlers from the Cayman Islands arrived in the 19th century, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> held the islands as a colony from 1852 to 1860, and tourism and diving now dominate its economy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roatan.jpg" alt="Roatán" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Westbrowncanada · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Westbay2106.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
